# Next.js / Nuxt coding style

Narrows `core-common-rules`' style rules to Next.js (App Router, React) and
Nuxt (Vue 3). Applies to `.tsx`/`.jsx` (Next.js) and `.vue` (Nuxt); a project
using one framework gets only that framework's guidance.

## File and directory naming

- Next.js App Router: `kebab-case` route segment folders (`app/order-history/page.tsx`); keep reserved file names (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `route.ts`) exactly as the framework requires.
- Nuxt: `kebab-case` files under `pages/` (`pages/order-history.vue`), dynamic segment `pages/orders/[id].vue`, catch-all `pages/[...slug].vue`; `PascalCase.vue` components.
- Composables (Nuxt) and hooks (Next.js/React) start with `use` (`useOrderTotals`), one export per file for a non-trivial one.

## Component and directive placement

- Next.js: put `'use client'` as the first line only in a file that itself needs browser state (`useState`, `useEffect`), event handlers, or a browser-only API, on the smallest leaf component that needs it, not because an ancestor or descendant does.
- Nuxt: use `<script setup lang="ts">` for new SFCs, not the Options API or a bare `<script>` with `defineComponent`.
- Type props explicitly: Next.js takes a typed `props` object (not `any`); Nuxt declares props with `defineProps<{ ... }>()`, not the runtime object form, beyond a trivial component.

## Imports and auto-imports

- Nuxt: do not hand-import what Nuxt auto-imports from `composables/`, `components/`, `utils/`; explicitly import anything outside those directories.
- Next.js: import explicitly, using the project's configured path aliases (`@/components/...`) over long relative chains.

## Formatting and typing

- Format with the project's configured formatter; do not hand-format around it.
- No `any` for props, route params, or fetch responses; type route params from Next.js's generated `PageProps` types (or the project's param type) and Nuxt's `useRoute().params` by name, not by casting.
- Do not share a barrel import file re-exporting both server-only code (`'use server'` files, Nuxt `server/` routes) and client-only code.
